      "dom_id": "question-47870",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "Given that $f(x)=3{x}^{2}$, what is ${f}^{′}(2)$ according to the definition?",
      "worked_solution": "The definition of ${f}^{′}(2)$ is\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to 2}(\\frac{f(x)-f(a)}{x-a}).\n$$\n\nLet $a=2.$ Then, we get\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to 2}(\\frac{3{x}^{2}-3(2)^{2}}{x-2}).\n$$",
